+# HST Office modules
+
+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary -->
+
+HST Office keeps the code of its own features here, apart from the LibreOffice code base. The LibreOffice files
+only call into it through thin hooks.
+
+## ribbon
+
+Ribbon customization and the recently used tab ("Sử dụng gần đây") of the Tabbed ribbon in Writer, Sheets,
+Slides and Draw.
+
+- `ribbon/core`: data and rules in standard C++ only. It includes no office or toolkit headers. It holds the JSON
+  reader and writer, the default and effective ribbon layouts, the customization file and its merge and diff, the
+  edits of the customize dialog, the usage history with its ranking, noise list and pruning, the usage store (the
+  recently used tab's switch and every app's history; switching the tab off keeps the history, only "Xóa lịch sử"
+  clears it), and the plan of the recently used tab. It is built as the static library `hst_ribbon_core` and unit tested by
+  `CppunitTest_hst_ribbon_core` (`qa/unit/ribbon-core-test.cxx`).
+- `ribbon/lo`: the adapter linked into sfx2.
+  - `ribbon-custom-controller`: reads the ribbon as built and applies the customization before its first layout.
+  - `ribbon-customize-dialog`: the "Tùy chỉnh ribbon" dialog, `sfx2/uiconfig/ui/hstribboncustomizedialog.ui`.
+  - `ribbon-usage-recorder`: records dispatched commands in batches.
+  - `ribbon-custom-service`: `vn.hasontech.hst.RibbonCustomization`, used by Tùy chọn › HST Office › Ribbon.
+  - `ribbon-ui-markup`: writes the `.ui` documents of custom groups and tabs in the ribbon's v3 group format.
+    It is standard C++, so it is part of the static library.
+  - `ribbon-custom-hooks.hxx`: the only header the LibreOffice files include.
+
+The user profile holds the files in `<user>/hst-ribbon/`:
+
+- `custom-<app>.json`: the change against the default ribbon. An entry that does not apply is skipped, and the
+  default stays.
+- `usage-<app>.json`: the local command history. It keeps 30 days and at most 300 commands.
+- `settings.json`: the recently used tab's switch.
